I reckon you can, mister.

00:55:37.520 --> 00:55:38.380
Right around behind.

00:55:38.750 --> 00:55:39.300
Come on.

00:55:46.210 --> 00:55:51.620
Oh, Mrs. Marlowe.

00:55:52.270 --> 00:55:52.670
Marlowe?

00:55:53.280 --> 00:55:56.010
Aren't you the congressman that was going to do so much for us ranchers?

00:55:56.360 --> 00:55:57.320
And then change your mind?

00:55:57.460 --> 00:56:00.000
Yes, but then conditions were misrepresented.

00:56:00.000 --> 00:56:02.980
You sure fixed it so I got to haul water 20 miles.

00:56:02.980 --> 00:56:05.790
None of you get it dropped.

00:56:05.790 --> 00:56:06.790
Oh, no, hold on.

00:56:10.840 --> 00:56:11.720
Hey, wait a minute.

00:56:11.720 --> 00:56:12.720
Listen, you can't do it.

00:56:12.720 --> 00:56:13.720
That's not right.

00:56:13.720 --> 00:56:14.720
We've got to have water.

00:56:14.720 --> 00:56:27.070
Please stop him.

00:56:27.070 --> 00:56:27.890
He has no right to refuse it.

00:56:27.890 --> 00:56:28.900
Just as much right as your company has to do it.

00:56:28.900 --> 00:56:30.000
Just as much right as your company has to do it.

00:56:30.000 --> 00:56:55.420
had to refuse the rancher's water the dust storm and it's coming our way dust storm what

00:56:55.420 --> 00:57:00.000
do we do you saw pictures of one mr. Marlowe now you're gonna see the real thing we've gotta

00:57:00.090 --> 00:57:02.500
Come on!

00:57:55.850 --> 00:57:57.090
Where's your husband, Mrs. Larkin?

00:57:57.190 --> 00:57:58.680
He's going to town for grub.

00:57:58.800 --> 00:58:00.000
He ought to be back pretty soon.

00:58:00.220 --> 00:58:01.300
Have you any water?

00:58:01.300 --> 00:58:05.660
We have some now, mister, but the cistern will be full of dust after this storm.

00:58:05.660 --> 00:58:09.900
Cistern? I thought you said the Great Western Pipeline ran through here.

00:58:09.900 --> 00:58:11.580
Well, I'd been informed.

00:58:11.580 --> 00:58:15.120
Of course, the water company wouldn't misinform anybody, would it, Andrews?

00:58:15.120 --> 00:58:17.020
The pump's in the corner, right over there.

00:58:17.020 --> 00:58:20.300
Help yourselves. Anything we've got here, you're welcome to.

00:58:24.740 --> 00:58:28.170
Do you have dust and ammonia out here, Rogers?

00:58:28.170 --> 00:58:30.000
No, you needn't worry.

00:58:30.060 --> 00:58:31.660
We don't even have dust storms here.

00:58:32.080 --> 00:58:34.280
They have them in another state, and you need to rub it in.

00:58:37.350 --> 00:58:41.640
I thought you were the one who wanted to see the dust storms.

00:59:22.430 --> 00:59:30.000
dust storms over what do we owe you mrs larkin man's sakes mister you don't owe me nothing roy paid me

00:59:30.000 --> 00:59:36.740
yesterday but we weren't here yesterday so the whole thing was a frame up eh everything with

00:59:36.740 --> 00:59:42.810
the dust arm that was an added attraction you mean the hold up and the water wagon were planned

00:59:42.810 --> 00:59:57.240
that's right i see nothing to laugh at young man i want to shake you by the hand

00:59:57.240 --> 01:00:00.000
your methods are not only unethical they're phenomenal

01:00:00.480 --> 01:00:04.400
But don't you worry. I'll okay that water bill.

01:00:04.400 --> 01:00:16.300
Thanks. The ranchers are headed to blow up the dam.

01:00:16.300 --> 01:00:19.780
Rogers, if they blast that dam, they'll lose government support.

01:00:19.780 --> 01:00:24.130
I'll stop 'em.

01:00:37.480 --> 01:00:39.760
I think it was Marlow. Head for the dam and step on it.

01:01:05.880 --> 01:01:07.740
All right, Bridget, thanks for the warning.

01:01:07.740 --> 01:01:08.740
We'll teach them a lesson.

01:02:30.030 --> 01:02:31.030
That'd stop 'em.

01:02:31.030 --> 01:02:33.030
We better stay here a while and make sure.

01:02:35.440 --> 01:02:48.820
- Steven! - Yes, we turned them back. They've gone over the hill.

01:02:48.820 --> 01:02:51.350
Come on, get back here and get down.

01:02:51.760 --> 01:02:59.670
We'll never get to the dam now. Unhook them horses.

01:03:03.930 --> 01:03:07.550
If you turn that dynamite wagon loose down that hill, blast the ditch and the water can't

01:03:07.550 --> 01:03:08.610
get to the dam.

01:03:08.610 --> 01:03:09.720
Get that wagon to roll 'em.

01:03:09.720 --> 01:03:17.770
That's the dynamite wagon.

01:03:17.770 --> 01:03:24.550
You better get out of here.

01:03:24.550 --> 01:03:29.030
No way.
